WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.840
Um, Supervisor?

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.730
Hm?

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.230
Did something happen to Number 15-kun?

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.610
Number 15?

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.130
He looks a bit dispirited,

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.120
like something is bothering him.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.940
Who knows?

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.700
Crap. Maybe I've come too far.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.590
I should start heading back.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.840
Rock?

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.180
Deputy Supervisor, welcome back.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.660
You're late!

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.320
Did Number 69-kun and the 
others return to their cell?

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.950
Hey, I heard you'd gone to Building 5.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.680
Where's Yamato?

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.070
Deputy Supervisor?!

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.450
Did you hear something just now?

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.670
Rock?

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.450
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.020
<b>Something Is Breaking</b>

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.680
What the hell are you thinking, Yamato?

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.780
Supervisor! Deputy Supervisor! Please stop!

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:15.380
R-Rock... This hurts!

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.240
What's wrong with you?

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.950
Did something happen?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.760
Or...

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.900
Oh, crap! I just organized those papers!

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.420
Now is no time to worry about that, sir!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.040
What if the deputy supervisor 
is seriously hurt?!

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.440
Don't worry. He's tough.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.490
That's not the point!

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.490
Deputy Supervisor! Are you all right?!

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.750
<i>He's the one who attacked me first.
Why am I getting yelled at?</i>

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.060
Anyway, it's strange.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:55.940
Hey, Seitarou.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:56.790
Yes?

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.500
About Yamato...

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.140
Why?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.610
I hope you'll discover
your favorite food soon.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.820
That gave me an even better idea.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.870
<i>Something is changing.</i>

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.870
<b>Something is changing</b>

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.380
Say something...

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.380
Please, say something!

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.690
What... happened to you?

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.510
Hey...

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.890
<b>Something is breaking</b>

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.170
<i>Something is breaking.</i>

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:51.390
Jyugo!

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.270
Jyugo! Rock! What the 
hell are you guys doing?!

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.580
Uno...

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:04.740
Wait! Did I do something to offend you?

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.820
If I did, I'm sorry. So...

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.410
No... You don't have to tell 
me if you don't want to.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.180
It's just that you, well...

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.580
don't seem like yourself. 
It's kinda worrying me.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.090
You're gonna go see Uno and the rest, right?

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:28.840
I wonder what's wrong?

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.850
Why aren't the guards coming?

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.030
You're not gonna hit them, right?

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.480
You won't... hurt anyone, right?

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.480
<b>Something is out of control</b>

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.480
<i>Something is out of control.</i>

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:48.140
You're... yourself, right?

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.370
Hey, Jyugo! What are you doing out there?!

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.940
What's wrong?! Hurry up and open the door!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.260
No... I won't open it.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.260
Don't be stupid! What are you saying?!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.220
Open it! Open the door! 
I'll take care of it, so let me out!

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:17.880
No, I... I have to take care of this somehow.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:21.770
Jyugo!

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.150
Jeez, what a pain in the ass.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.510
What's with him all of a sudden, anyway?

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.500
What's this?

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:47.530
Tsukumo...

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.330
Tsukumo-kun?

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.320
Didn't he go to Building 5, too?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.160
Tsukumo, why?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.560
Did something happen to you, too?!

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:59.760
Answer me, Tsukumo!

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.310
You're yourself, right?!

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.260
Right, Tsukumo?!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.920
What's with that face, Jyugo?

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:12.110
You're the one who said, "Be yourself."

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.120
So I'm my usual self.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:19.880
On the way back from Building 5, 
Yamato-san and Rock seemed oddly quiet.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.540
I thought it was strange, so I followed him.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.880
Something happened in Building 5?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:24.500
I don't know.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:27.350
But if Rock is like this,

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.240
I'm certain Yamato-san is, too.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.490
If the same thing is happening 
in the guard room,

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.240
it explains why no one's coming.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.190
Sorry. I couldn't do anything...

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.020
I didn't know what to do,

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.770
but I wanted to help him.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:45.850
Yet in the end, I couldn't stop Rock.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.900
All I could think about was 
what was in front of me.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.610
The more I thought about it,

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.530
I thought I was the reason...

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.910
That was... the only thing I could think of.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:02.290
This is happening... because I'm here.

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:07.320
Maybe I shouldn't be here.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.120
Jyugo...

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.420
Tsukumo, behind you!

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:22.560
I don't know why you think it's your fault.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.080
I don't know what happened,

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.220
but you're not yourself today.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:29.570
You're lost, because you're 
afraid of something.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:30.680
Huh?

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:33.100
You thought this was unusual.

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.320
That something was off.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.580
I think it's good that you even realize that.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.820
Rather than thinking about what you can do,

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.710
isn't it more important that 
you <i>want</i> to do something?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:53.380
I knew very well that you wanted 
to stop Rock and tried to help him.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.900
So I wanted to do something, too.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.200
I didn't think too much before acting.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.140
Just like you.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.890
Don't think. Feel.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.900
Just think about how Uno and Nico feel.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.720
They know more about the 
two of you than I do.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.530
Hey, Jyugo, Tsukumo.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.040
There's something on the 
back of Rock's neck.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.220
Like a talisman or something.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:21.990
A talisman?

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.500
Tsukumo!

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:32.670
Rock!

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.810
Stop this already...

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.370
Please.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.860
Rock?

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.470
<b>Command</b>

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.470
This talisman looks... familiar.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.230
I've seen this before.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.100
<b>Nanba Building 5</b>

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.350
Huh? The talismans...

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.260
They're gone.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:31.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:36.990
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.490
<b>Infirmary</b>

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.370
Jeez, what the hell is 
wrong with Building 13?

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:55.260
All of you coming here so late at night...

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:57.550
You'd better stay in bed until morning.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.750
Take care.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:04.380
Rock isn't awake yet, huh?

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:11.270
Doc said he's just sleeping and 
doesn't seem to be hurt or sick.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.630
It's the same story with Yamato-chan.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.900
Seitarou-chan is getting treated right now.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.800
It suddenly got all quiet...

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.580
What was that talisman about?

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.660
Yamato, who was nearly killed 
by Hajime, had one too, I heard.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.160
Rock stopped moving once 
it was removed, right?

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.200
Yeah.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.010
I think I've seen that talisman before.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:35.890
Really?

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.570
Where was it?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.550
That talisman is probably from Building 5.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:43.060
I've seen the same one many times,

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.180
and I've heard about how it's used, as well.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.430
Tsukumo, are you all right?

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.430
They said I have no broken bones.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.560
But I should've practiced 
breaking my falls a bit more.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.260
Hm? What's wrong?

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.590
Nothing, just... Were you 
always this type of character?

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:01.840
You don't talk like a ninja.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.290
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.900
<i>The normal me slipped out!</i>

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:07.780
<i>How embarrassing!</i>

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.670
Are you not really a ninja?!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.410
Huh?! No, I meant...

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.830
What?! Tsukumo-kun, you're not a ninja?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.610
U-Um, well...

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.400
You're not a Japanese ninja?!

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.100
It's a long story, you see...

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:24.590
<i>This scene kinda brings back memories.</i>

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.470
Rock wasn't himself.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:33.100
At the least, he wasn't the Rock we know.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:39.780
It seems Building 5's talisman is a special 
object handled using the owner's chi.

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:44.750
For someone who can use qigong, like Upa,

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.910
I heard it can suppress or control his power.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.540
Hold on a minute.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.160
Neither Rock nor Yamato 
can use qigong, though.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:54.880
This is just a theory,

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:59.090
but if the talisman is powerful enough 
to control someone who can use qigong,

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:03.420
wouldn't it be even easier
to control a normal person?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.000
Are you saying someone 
was controlling them?

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.000
Oh? What's wrong?

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.180
You're in the break room at this hour?

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:16.200
I could say the same to you.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:19.540
I'm heading back after turning 
in some important paperwork.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.420
Do you know where the monkey is?

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:23.440
I came here to see him.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.530
Hey, you're not planning 
to fight again, are you?

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.220
No. I just wanted to ask him about this.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.950
Oh, that's the talisman 
they use in Building 5, right?

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.160
I'm a bit concerned about this,

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.210
so I wanted to ask him directly.

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:41.160
Well, if you see the monkey, can you
tell him I'm going to Building 5 tomorrow?

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:44.180
Why should I? You tell him yourself.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.590
You're gonna see him anyway, 
so what's the big deal?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:49.590
Besides, I can't get a hold of him.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:56.420
Let's say that Building 5's 
talisman is behind all this.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.480
We still don't know who used them,

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.360
or why they decided to control those two.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:06.610
Yamato and Rock aren't all that stupid, so it
wouldn't be that easy to place one on them.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.780
You're right.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:10.700
To attach the talisman on 
a location so well-hidden...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.520
They normally would've resisted.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.170
You were with them,

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.500
so why aren't you affected?

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.800
That's been bothering me, too.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:21.720
There was no mention of the talisman 
while I was in Building 5.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:23.710
If I remember correctly, I was...

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:27.380
focused on training and stayed outside.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.640
This all makes less and less sense.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.680
<i>Building 5's talisman...</i>

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.630
<i>If something happened to Rock 
because he was at Building 5,</i>

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.890
<i>is that the source?</i>

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:44.160
<i>If something like this happens again, I'll...</i>

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.280
Then how about this?

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:56.180
Since it's pointless to argue
about who did it and why,

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:58.560
shouldn't we just go to Building 5 ourselves?

00:14:58.880 --> 00:14:59.660
Huh?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.300
No!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.680
Why not?!

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:10.970
Isn't it obvious?

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:14.190
I can't just take inmates to another building!

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:17.310
That's what you called me 
this early in the morning for?

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.550
What's the big deal?!

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.880
You're about to go to Building 5 anyway.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.810
Take us with you.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.660
Who told you that?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:26.480
You think Yamato and Rock were acting crazy

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.190
because they went to Building 5, right?

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.950
We've been thinking that, too.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:35.700
We have the right to know 
what happened to Rock

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.970
and what the hell is going on.

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:41.580
We won't rest until we see 
the truth with our own eyes.

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:42.910
Idiot.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.340
You punks have no part in this.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.960
It's our job.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.440
Stay out of our way.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:53.720
Hmm... I guess it can't be helped.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.470
We'll just go on our own, then.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:02.070
I asked you out of the goodness 
of my heart, you know.

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.140
It seems like you're too busy right now,

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.360
since Yamato and Seitarou 
are out of commission.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:10.650
I pleaded with you because it felt wrong

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.240
to increase your workload
if it wasn't necessary.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:18.490
Did you forget that we're 
the best jailbreakers around?

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.970
You think you can get out of here?

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:23.580
Of course. We have Jyugo.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:26.120
You know that better than anyone, right?

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:35.460
So who will suffer the most if 
we get out and cause trouble?

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:37.270
Are you threatening me?

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:39.070
I'm not threatening you.

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:41.050
We asked kindly,

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.620
but you turned us down.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.140
So I'm telling you.

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:45.900
This is a deal.

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:50.460
A deal is made when both
sides have something to gain.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:53.360
What do I gain by taking you punks with me?

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.650
That's a loss for me.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.880
I only make deals that benefit me.

00:16:57.890 --> 00:16:59.880
That's not really a deal.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:02.080
The warden is gone too, right?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.660
It's a huge opportunity, don't you think?

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:06.040
You know about that, too?

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.760
Uno-kun is amazing.
He's negotiating with Hajime-chan!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:12.050
<b>Grin Grin</b>

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:12.050
This sort of thing is his forte.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.080
So what's it gonna be?

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.420
Are you taking us or not?

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:20.310
Are you willing to bet that nothing 
will happen if you leave us here?

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.960
<i>He's right. It's dangerous 
to leave them here.</i>

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.310
<i>They're unpredictable.</i>

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:33.570
<b>But if I just take Number 15, the other two probably won't just wait patiently.</b>

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:30.340
<i>But if I just take Number 15,</i>

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:33.570
<i>the other two probably
won't just wait patiently.</i>

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:41.580
<b>If they do anything worse than escaping,
my ass is on the line.
Yamato and Seitarou are getting medical treatment,
so I can't have them watch Cell 13 for me.</b>

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:35.560
<i>If they do anything worse than escaping,</i>

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:37.420
<i>my ass is on the line.</i>

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.600
<i>Yamato and Seitarou are 
getting medical treatment,</i>

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.580
<i>so I can't have them watch Cell 13 for me.</i>

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:49.080
<b>Even if I ask the other guards for help, I'm the only one who can catch them.
Number 11 even knows where the traps are.</b>

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:43.890
<i>Even if I ask the other guards for help,</i>

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:46.700
<i>I'm the only one who can catch them.</i>

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:49.080
<i>Number 11 even knows where the traps are.</i>

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.290
<i>If he activates them again,</i>

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.340
<i>headquarters will surely find out this time.</i>

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:56.080
<i>But how do I know they won't 
cause trouble if I take them?</i>

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.100
Hmm...

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:04.100
<b>Hmm
Hmm</b>

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:01.740
Hmm... Hmm...

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:03.710
Hurry up!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.850
<b>10 Minutes Later</b>

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.610
All right. Just this once!

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.280
Woohoo!

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:14.230
<b>Wow</b>

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:13.970
Wow...

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:15.340
Amazing!

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.110
<b>Amazing</b>

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.110
But...

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.810
If you cause any trouble,

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:20.260
you know what'll happen, right?

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.620
Y-Yes, sir.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.500
Yay!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.830
Jeez... I hope nothing happens.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.830
<b>5</b>

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:34.340
<b>Nanba Building 5</b>

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:46.020
Wow! So this is Building 5, huh? Ritzy.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.820
I've only ever seen anything like this in manga!

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:50.600
Hm? Nico, what's that?

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.630
It's a bag for my medications.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.740
Seitarou-chan made it for me.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.800
Right... Seitarou-chan...

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.830
He was a good guy.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.870
He's not dead.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.120
<b>Nanba Building 5</b>

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.560
Hey, Mitsuru.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:12.770
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:14.750
Give me a status report on Building 5.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:18.880
Can't you sound a little more 
lovable when you ask that?

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:23.950
I came all the way to Building 13 to 
keep an eye on it for you, y'know.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:25.040
<i>Shut up.</i>

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:27.120
<i>It doesn't seem like anyone's here.</i>

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:28.890
<i>Can you contact the guards inside?</i>

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.860
Oh, you haven't heard?

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:35.500
We did contact the guys at Building 5,

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:38.160
but nobody has responded.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.080
But as far as I can see in there,

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.660
everything looks normal.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:43.660
Except...

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.410
<i>Except?</i>

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.580
I don't see any guards at all.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.640
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:52.020
Hey, it's your job to find that out today.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:55.030
Anyway, I'll be waiting to hear back from ya.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.040
That pompous ass...

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.840
<i>By the way, why is there a cat—</i>

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.800
Sorry, I'm losing you!

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.790
How does this open?

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:06.160
Can you open it?

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:07.400
Probably.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:12.190
It opened.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.880
Hey, don't open it without permission!

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.290
I didn't do anything!

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.070
It opened on its own!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.580
<i>It definitely feels like there's no one here.</i>

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:31.890
What...

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.310
What the hell is this?!

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:35.680
Did you punks touch something?!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.000
We didn't do anything!

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:40.120
You're stupid enough to fall into 
a trap without doing something?!

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:41.230
Actually...

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:46.470
You're the one who fell into a trap.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.720
Why?!

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:53.230
You're like a gorilla in a cage!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.230
<b>Forever gorilla</b>

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.770
What a riot!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.850
Number 11, I'll kill you!

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.860
Damn it! This is nothing.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:02.270
Huh?

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:08.080
Now you're handcuffed! What an idiot!

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.340
Hajime-chan, are you trying 
to make us laugh?!

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:12.260
You look so funny!

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:13.880
Why would I try to make you laugh?!

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.120
I'll kill you little shits!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.260
Cage and handcuffs? Seriously?! No way!

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:21.150
Only inmates look good 
in a cage and handcuffs.

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:22.450
This doesn't make any sense.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:23.380
Enough already!

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:27.140
If you don't like it, why don't you 
try to get out, Hajime-cha... n?

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.510
Hajime-cha... n?

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:29.990
Hajime-cha... n?

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:34.020
<b>Aaaaahhhhhhhh</b>

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:36.680
Serves you right.

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.990
You're not worried about us?!

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:44.650
You were caught pretty easily.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:47.410
What's the meaning of this?

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.480
'Sup.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:28.160
After we fell into the hole,

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:30.470
we woke up in an underground cell?!

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:32.680
Huh? Master and Liang?
What are you two doing here?

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:36.060
And what is that disgusting thing?!

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:37.010
Next episode:

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>You Are Weak</b>

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:38.600
"You Are Weak."
